[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163178655","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/695#issuecomment-163178655","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/695","id":163178655,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE2MzE3ODY1NQ==","user":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-11-04T16:37:49Z","updated_at":"2015-12-09T10:19:43Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **BitBucket: [dmand](http://bitbucket.org/dmand), GitHub: @dmand?**:\n\n---\n\nThanks for the report.\n\nSo the problem is that unpacking checker goes through all the possible inferred values of right-hand side of the assignment expression. In the case of `Test` class it has two possible values: tuple `(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)` and `None`. So checker sees that `None` is a possible value (even though it comes from an overridden method) and emits an error. And in the case of `Test2` class there is only one infered value, `(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)`, so error is not emitted.\n\nI'm not sure what the best approach to fixing this bug is. I have a few ideas:\n1. Check unpacking only if there is only one possible value inferred (aka use `helpers.safe_infer())\n2. Investigate why inference of `self.test(None)` inside class `Test` yields two possible values and make it not yield a value of base class method call.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163178655/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163178656","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/695#issuecomment-163178656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/695","id":163178656,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE2MzE3ODY1Ng==","user":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.